{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1508548-weak-spots-edge-\u2013-is-overpowered","id":1508548,"title":"Weak Spots Edge \u2013 Is overpowered?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-16T12:01:18-07:00","id":1508548,"title":"Weak Spots Edge \u2013 Is overpowered?","content":"So I feel my Assassins players are a bit overusing <b><i>Weak Spots </i>Edge. </b>They conviced me they can re-roll once any roll each Story Milestone - i.e. session, maybe two. Re-reading Edge, I assume it's only for Complex Rolls rerolls&gt;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>'TC Core, p. </strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">WEAK SPOTS (\u2022)<br /> It\u2019s better to catch a flaw early, before something \u2014 or someone \u2014 gets hurt. Your character has an eye for weaknesses in materials, or can spot errors in blueprints and calculations. Once per milestone, she may reroll a failed attempt or ignore a single Complication.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-17-2023, 05:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T12:11:52-07:00","id":1508551,"title":"","content":"That's how it works. 1 re-roll each session. I allow it to be used once a session on any failed roll. Has never felt OP to me and I have a player that makes a point of taking it on almost every character she makes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T15:36:28-07:00","id":1508574,"title":"","content":"The examples provided in the second sentence make it seem like the Edge is meant to apply to Complex Rolls, which means that when it applies, they should be using it a lot more than once per session, which really does seem overpowered.<br /> <br /> For example, pg. 78 provides &quot;hacking a secure network&quot; as a task that may require four milestones and 5 minutes per roll. That means each of the four attempts can be rerolled once should they fail, and the player can ignore a single complication of their choice if no reroll is needed for that milestone.<br /> <br /> Other complex actions that would benefit would be item crafting, forming/renewing bonds, and prolonged car chases. Basically, any action that requires more than a single roll would theoretically benefit. As long as the Difficulty isn't too high or the dicepool too small, the character should almost never fail a milestone, and they'd often have extra successes for stunts since they can outright ignore a single complication of their choice.<br /> <br /> Overall, claiming the milestone is specifically a story milestone and the Edge can apply once per session makes much more sense. Spending 2-3 xp for an Edge that lets you reroll anything/ignore one complication once per session sounds okay to me, while letting that same Edge affect every single complex action would be kind of absurd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}